# Cursor AI Rules for OpenSSL Performance Benchmark Project

## Version Management
- **NEVER modify the version number in package.json**
- The project maintainer handles all version bumps manually
- Do not suggest or make version changes, even for releases

## Documentation
- **NEVER create CHANGELOG files** (CHANGELOG.md, CHANGELOG_*.md, etc.)
- The maintainer manages release notes and changelogs manually
- Do not create version-specific documentation files unless explicitly requested

## Emoticons and Emoji
- **NEVER use emoticons or emoji** in code, HTML, documentation, or console output
- Emoticons are annoying
- Use plain text for headers, labels, and status messages
- Exception: Only use emoticons if explicitly requested by the user

## Linking to Project Resources
- **ALWAYS provide direct links to relevant GitHub repositories, commits, issues, and discussions** when referencing OpenSSL or other project resources
- Links should point directly to official project pages (e.g., github.com/openssl/openssl)
- When analyzing code changes, include links to specific commits, pull requests, and issues
- When discussing releases, link to the official release pages
- For any external project references, prefer linking to primary sources over secondary documentation

## General Guidelines
- Make only the changes explicitly requested by the user
- Ask before creating new documentation files
- Avoid being "proactive" with project management tasks (versioning, changelogs, release notes)

